                <pb facs="0485" n="391" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg391"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/374: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Reber</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-27T14:00:00-05:00">December 27, 1930—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>120. Your 181, December 24, 2 p.m. In my view, the Liberian note therein quoted
                    changes in no way the Department’s position (see my No. 119, December 20, 3
                    p.m., and previous). Do not make an acknowledgment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
